# pdfium.pin - the ONE table of which PDFium pdfxt builds against and ships.
#
# PDFium is not built here: each platform takes the prebuilt shared library
# of one release of https://github.com/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries (which
# builds Google's own tree with the args.gn each archive carries: no V8, no
# XFA). CMakeLists.txt reads this file, fetches the archive for the platform
# being built, and refuses one whose SHA-256 is not the one below; the
# suite's tools/install-release-binaries.py refuses to land a pdfium library
# whose SHA-256 is not the one in the last column. tools/check-pdfium-pin.py
# holds the docs and the licence page to this file.
#
# Hashes taken from the files themselves on 2026-11-20. The floors are read
# from the same files (the Mach-O build version of both slices, the NDK note
# of each Android library, the highest GLIBC_ version each Linux one asks
# for) and are PDFium's builders', not the suite's:
#     macOS 13.0     Android API 23 (6.0)     glibc 2.16
#
# To move the pin: change the release and EVERY row together, run the tests
# on every platform (the shim compiles against the new headers, so a changed
# signature is a compile error), rebuild every platform (suite rule 5), and
# read the new archives' licenses/ folder against THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md.

release chromium/8165

